  "notes": "After winning the opening lead, South's only problem is not losing 2 trump tricks. South does have 2 heart losers, but Dummy's clubs can eventually be used to take care of those losers.\n\nSouth has an almost certain way of playing the spade suit for only 1 loser. South should cash the ♠A or ♠K. When both defenders follow small, South should lead a low spade towards the ♠J in dummy. This plan will always work unless West was dealt all 5 spades. If East has all 5 spades the second round of spades must come from the dummy.\n\nOn the above distribution, for example, West will show out on the second spade lead towards the ♠J. East will win the ♠Q, but a finessing position exists over East's ♠10. After drawing trump, South can discard his heart losers on North's clubs.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "After winning the opening lead, South's only problem is not losing 2 trump tricks. South does have 2 heart losers, but Dummy's clubs can eventually be used to take care of those losers.",
